+/* [GT6 0149] A CUBE TEXTURE WHOSE SIX FACES ARE SIX RENDER TARGETS OF THEIR OWN. Gran Turismo 6's "additional light"
+ * maps (the shader's additionalLightMap0 .. 3) are the light each car throws - the head lamps' beam white ahead of it,
+ * the tail lamps red behind - as a 32x32 cube of 16-bit floats; the title draws each face into a 32x32 target of its
+ * own, face f at the cube's address + f x (pitch x height), and every road and scenery draw binds four such cubes. A
+ * cube texture that sits on a surface is decoded from guest memory (see the bind) unless one surface holds all of
+ * it (surface_cube_window: the reflection map, A8R8G8B8 with border texels) - and nothing copies those float targets
+ * into guest memory: the four cubes read as black. No lamp lit the road at night.
+ * Here such a cube is a host cube texture filled from its six face surfaces by GPU copies whenever one of them has
+ * been written since the last fill (not while the draw's own target is one of the faces: a cube is not read while
+ * it is being drawn). Plain cubes only - no border texels in the data, one level, a square face of A8R8G8B8 or
+ * W16Z16Y16X16 float - and only where all six faces are surfaces of that size and format; otherwise as before.
+ * LD_CUBE_FACES=0: as before. */
+#define LD_SWIN_CUBE_FACES 0x100u
